// Base64 PNG of the full logo lockup (1158x750), straight from
// public/email/mark.png (already verified correct via direct byte-equality
// check against that file). Embedded as a Postmark inline attachment
// (ContentID 'logo', referenced via src="cid:logo" in api/submit-form.js)
// instead of linked by URL — a linked https://swiftowl.ai/... image breaks
// the moment that domain points somewhere else (it served the old WordPress
// site, not this deployment, at one point), and an inline attachment has no
// such dependency: it's embedded in the email itself.
//
// This is deliberately NOT a browser-canvas-downscaled smaller version —
// two separate attempts to shrink it via canvas.toDataURL() silently
// produced blank/corrupted image data despite the canvas itself holding
// correct pixels (confirmed via getImageData), a reproducible browser-
// automation quirk. Embedding the full ~268KB file directly, with zero
// canvas involvement, sidesteps that class of bug entirely. Postmark's
// attachment limits are generous; this size is a non-issue.
export const LOGO_PNG_BASE64 = ''
